<http://data.silknow.org/object/c28a3b7a-51d9-3d09-a80d-c507afe94294/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Towel/Napkin, cotton embroidered with silk in double darning, double running in a line and musabak stitch, and with plate in musabak and padded satin stitch.\nThe narrow border along the ends and up the sides of the border is worked in metal thread.The border consists of two alternating motifs, both worked in metal thread: a small building on a mound and a large structure which resembles a minbar.  Above and below these are predominantly dark pink and red flowers.  There are some small cypress trees and isolated sprigs below.\nOne side has been cut and hemmed"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/c28a3b7a-51d9-3d09-a80d-c507afe94294> .

<http://data.silknow.org/image/71962e4c-eba7-3996-97aa-3d301f21da5d>
        a                  ecrm:E38_Image ;
